From 07c34a4b7cff1e361441b18bd23421d35f376a94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joethedev5 <deepsbx1@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:56:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Recover bsd/net/observability.c

Reconstruct the network observability unit from the KDK 27.0.1 DWARF and
the RELEASE and kasan vmapple kernels: the parent-chain result enum and
info record, the development-only log handle, the observability sysctls
and all six functions of the unit.

check_parent_chain() walks the parent chain from proc_ppid() and
proc_uniqueid() up to launchd, bounded at 63 levels, and stops at the
first untrusted ancestor.  It detects pid reuse and cycles by comparing
the uniqueid of the process found for ppid against the child's uniqueid,
records the pid and command name of the offending process, honors the
network observer entitlement when asked (clearing the chain and setting
entitled_ancestor), and treats platform binaries and Developer ID signed
third-party binaries as trusted.

net_check_observability_permission_impl() allows root; under lockdown
mode it allows only platform binaries with a clean chain, without
honoring the entitlement; otherwise it allows entitled tasks,
third-party bundles (cs_identity_get(), a non-empty identity containing
a dot and not prefixed by "com.apple.") with a Developer ID category,
unsigned third-party bundles with a clean chain (entitlement honored),
and platform binaries with a clean chain.  Everything else is denied.
process_can_see_connections() short-circuits on the
net_inet_hide_pcb_established switch and passes the source file name as
the log prefix; net_observability_should_hide_socket() keeps a socket
visible to its current process (last_pid/e_pid) and hides it otherwise.

The sysctls are the net.observability node, the always-present
net_rt_filter_cloned_routes and net_inet_hide_pcb_established defaults
(1), the development-only logging switch, the per-filter switches and
the privacy_enhancements master switch, which writes one value to the
route filter, MAC address filter and TCP connection-hiding switches
together.

The file compiles with the reference RELEASE flags and with the
DEVELOPMENT+DEBUG configuration; the statement line anchors match the
KDK line tables (Apple clang attributes some comparisons to a different
column than clang 19, as in the other recovered units).

Authored-By: joethedev5 <joeshmo@nunya.com>
